 154: RESULT per fault row (the classifier tests the STOP channel before pc, deliberately: the naive fix
 155: sets pc = entry and THEN stops, so pc alone cannot tell it from delivery):
 156:   HALT       `unimplemented vector=` printed AND the machine stopped (both observed, pass 3); an
 157:              expected-HALT row (resid50, resid127, sfu1h, usfu1) must also see ITS vector named in the diagnostic
 158:   TAILHALT   `internal error` printed and the machine stopped (the naive fix's shape)
 159:   STOP       the machine stopped for another reason (e.g. a wrong vector base landed in zeros)
 160:   BADREGS    the entry breakpoint fired but a shadow-register/PSR/destination assert failed, or (bad=refatal) the re-route's
 161:              `[ SFRZ already set in PSR => ERROR ]' line was present on a frozen-TRAP row or absent on a re-routed err* row --
 162:              the channel that separates the exemption arm from the re-route arm when both deliver to 0x50 (kimi, pass 6), or
 163:              (bad=level) the transcript carried an `exception <CLASS>' line: the class printed at ERROR
 164:              level, which the fork's default WARNING verbosity shows and INFO does not (kills M_LEVEL)
 165:   (rows resid50, resid127, sfu1h and usfu1 EXPECT HALT: the fallback stopping the machine is the correct answer there)
 166:   DELIVER    entry breakpoint fired, machine running, and every assert holds:
 167:              pc == entry, SXIP == fault_pc|V, SNIP, SFIP, PSR == 0x8000000b (SFRZ|IND|SFD1|MODE),
 168:              EPSR == the pre-fault PSR (0x80000002 supervisor rows; 0x00000002 user-mode rows),
 169:              r2 unchanged (0xdeadbeef)
 170:   NOSTART    the liveness marker never ran
 171: Controls print DONE (r2 == the expected quotient, machine running) or a failure word.
 172: 
 173: Output: one `M88KEXC_ROW=<name> RESULT=<word> ...` line per row, `M88KEXC_RESULT=<delivered>/<fault rows>`,
 174: `M88KEXC_SELFTEST=OK|FAIL`, `M88KEXC_DONE`.  Set M88KEXC_VERBOSE=1 for transcripts.
 175: 
 176: CONTRACT (clause e): catches a class returned to the fallback (HALT) by either route (instruction rows
 177: and the *tb trap rows); a SHRUNK fallback window (resid127 pins the far bound: `< 128' -> `< 127' or `< 51' both deliver 127 to the
 178: tail default, TAILHALT; usertb pins that 128 is outside it, resid50 the interior); a class reaching the tail default (TAILHALT); a wrong vector SCALING (M_VEC4,
 179: M_VEC7: STOP) and a DROPPED vector base (vbrtb: STOP); a stale SXIP/SNIP/SFIP; a wrong PSR, including a
 180: cleared carry (ovfc); a dropped IND (indclr); the debugmsg LEVEL regression to ERROR/WARNING (bad=level on any
 181: delivered row: those print at the post-startup WARNING floor, INFO and DEBUG do not -- so exact INFO is NOT pinned,
 182: only 'not ERROR/WARNING' -- M_LEVEL; codex, pass 3); a skipped EPSR save; a skipped supervisor switch (the user-mode rows: EPSR MODE
 183: clear vs PSR MODE set); a MODE-conditioned `implemented' on any class that user mode can raise ({class} x
 184: {MODE} closure: DIV0 udiv0, PRIVILEGE priv/privtb, UNIMPLEMENTED unimpl, MISALIGNED umisalign, OVERFLOW uovf;
 185: BOUNDS and ERROR have no user-mode route -- a user tb1 naming them raises PRIVILEGE, and every handler runs
 186: supervisor; the FALLBACK predicate itself is pinned in user mode by usfu1, the one user-mode route to it); a class-conditioned SFRZ re-route, its diagnostic pinned both ways by the refatal channel, and a PSR-bit conjunct on the re-route (the
 187: predicate reads PSR: every stcr-settable 88100 bit now varies there -- MODE errpriv, SFD1 errdiv0, IND errind, C errc; MXM/BO cannot be
 188: set by stcr without stopping the cpu, and SER is NOT an 88110-only bit -- mc88100.txt, anchor `SER - Serial Mode', documents it
 189: for the MC88100 as software-settable and m88k_stcr stores it verbatim, so trapfrozenser rows it.  *** AND THE CONFIGURATION CLAIM
 190: THIS DOCSTRING USED TO MAKE WAS FALSE TWICE OVER: it said the 88110-only bits `are 88100 here', and this probe launches
 191: `-E testm88k' with NO `-C', while machine_test.c's MACHINE_DEFAULT_CPU(testm88k) sets cpu_name to "88110".  Every table this
 192: round has run measured an 88110.  The SCORES stand -- nothing in the m88k model reads cpu_type to change behaviour outside the
 193: name and the PID register, so the exception path is shared -- but the CLAIM did not, and pinning `-C 88100' with a PID control
 194: row is owed as its own revision with its own BASE run (codex, pass 8). ***) ({SFRZ set, !is_trap} x {class}: MISALIGNED error, OVERFLOW errovf,
 195: DIV0 errdiv0 -- the handler clears SFD1 first, with it set the divu raises SFU1 instead (sfu1h) --, PRIVILEGE errpriv
 196: and UNIMPLEMENTED errunimpl -- the handler drops to user mode keeping SFRZ; BOUNDS and ERROR have no non-trap route,
 197: the frozen TRAP is trapfrozen); a wrong return address; the delay-slot else-arm's SFIP source (dslot, +16
 198: geometry); a delay-slot-conditioned `implemented' on any class a guest INSTRUCTION can raise from a delay slot ({class} x
 199: {delay slot} closure, v22: DIV0 dslot, MISALIGNED dslotmisalign, UNIMPLEMENTED dslotunimpl, PRIVILEGE dslotpriv, OVERFLOW
 200: dslotovf -- `implemented = !cpu->delay_slot' at the four latter arms swept v21 59/59, delayslot_20261016/, and the body's own
 201: `if (cpu->delay_slot)' is what makes delay_slot a floor axis.  v23 then closed the whole CLASS, because passes 13 and 14
 202: each found cells of it open (repair 14, the class-closure rule), as Fable 5.1 enumerated it on pass 14: the delivery path
 203: TESTS PSR & SFRZ and cpu->delay_slot, so the floor is {7 labels} x {SFRZ} x {delay_slot}, 28 cells, all rowed -- the
 204: (SFRZ clear, slot) column by the five rows above plus dslotbounds and dsloterror (a tb1 naming 7 / 10 in a slot, pinned as
 205: this emulator behaves: the MC88100 manual does not define a trap in a slot, and manual silence decides what a row may
 206: CLAIM, not whether the cell is owed); the (SFRZ set, slot) column by errdslotmisalign, errdslotovf, errdslotdiv0,
 207: errdslotpriv, errdslotunimpl, trapfrozen7dslot and trapfrozen10dslot (line 865's write is what X(br_n) reads to keep the
 208: vector over the branch target); and the fallback, clause (e) but rowed on its measured escape, by usfu1dslot.  Table 19
 209: (artifacts/m88kexcdeliver/repair13_20261016/).  Still disclosed, clause (e): a frozen TRAP in a slot at the five instruction
 210: labels (`if (!is_trap || (vector == L && cpu->delay_slot))', measured as escapes in table 19), {delay slot} x {a PSR bit
 211: other than SFRZ}, three-or-more-axis joints, and vectors 0..3's own delay-slot code (upstream, m88kexchwtraps)); a trap re-routed to ERROR while frozen, per class ({SFRZ set, is_trap} x {every switch-1 label a trap can NAME -- 0..3 are deliverable too and are unrowed, disclosed as
 212: m88kexchwtraps; the word EVERY overclaimed until v16}: trapfrozen (7),
 213: trapfrozen4/5/6/8/9/10/128/450/496/511 -- the ten labels 4..10, 128, 0x1c2, MVMEPROM_VECTOR, enumerated from switch 1's `case' list, plus
 214: the far edge of the user range (511) --
 215: class 10's re-route exemption is told from the re-route by the refatal channel (the pass-6 packet called it equivalent; kimi refuted
 216: that: the re-route prints a diagnostic the exemption does not) and switch 1's ERROR eligibility under SFRZ by trapfrozen10's
 217: HALT/DELIVER; 0..3 are the hardware-event tails, m88kexchwtraps); the fallback window's NEAR bound (resid11) and the fallback predicate
 218: conditioned on any settable PSR bit (resid50ind, resid50c, resid50ser, usfu1, sfu1h -- SIX bits, and resid50ser is
 219: what made that claim true when SER turned out to be settable); a written destination.  Does NOT catch:
 220: fcr2/fcr4/fcr5; scoreboard (SSBR) bits; DMT contents; the post-delivery
 221: `cpu->delay_slot' write on the NON-delay path (M_DELAYALWAYS: needs a second UNFROZEN exception -- filed);
 222: vectors 0..3's tail arms (no row: M_TAILOFF -- filed); vectors 11..113 and 116..127 (fallback halts by
 223: design); SFU1 (114/115, row m88kexcsfu1); `implemented = is_trap' on BOUNDS/ERROR (EQUIVALENT today: no
 224: instruction raises 7 or 10 -- becomes live when tbnd lands, row m88ktbnd); a PSR-bit conjunct on a switch-1 `implemented' arm
 225: OTHER than MODE (closed for every class) and SFRZ at ERROR (both polarities: errortb unfrozen, trapfrozen10 frozen) -- the arms read no PSR
 226: bit, so {arm} x {C, IND, SFD1} is clause-(e) debt, not floor; the representative (MISALIGNED with `!(PSR & C)', M_MISNOC) MEASURED
 227: 41/41 on v10 (the escape, as disclosed) and 45/46 on v14 -- KILLED by errc, whose second fault is MISALIGNED with C set (table 11).  So the
 228: {MISALIGNED} x {C} and {MISALIGNED} x {IND} cells are rowed by errc / errind as a side effect of the re-route rows; the disclosure stands
 229: for the remaining arms -- and that sentence was WRONG THREE WAYS until v16, all three measured (opus5, pass 8): it named
 230: OVERFLOW, which ovfc and indclr already close, since both fault at that arm with C set and IND clear respectively; it
 231: claimed {any arm} x {SFD1}, closed at all seven (at DIV0 architecturally -- X(divu) tests SFD1 BEFORE the divisor, so only
 232: the tb1 route reaches that arm with SFD1 set); and it OMITTED BOUNDS and ERROR, which were open.  v16 closes
 233: {UNIMPL, PRIV, BOUNDS, DIV0, ERROR} x {C, IND} with five rows and the re-route's trap side with three.  The DENOMINATOR is 7 arms x SIX settable bits (8 architectural
 234: minus BO and MXM, which the store path refuses) = 42 cells, minus the 2 MODE-unreachable at BOUNDS/ERROR = 40 -- v16 said 35
 235: and five bits, and grok corrected both on pass 9.  Those two ARE unreachable rather than merely unrowed: neither constant is
 236: raised by any instruction, a user tb1 naming a vector below 128 raises PRIVILEGE with is_trap == 0, and the re-route writes
 237: ERROR after switch 1 so it never enters that arm -- a warrant that EXPIRES when X(tbnd) lands (row m88ktbnd).  The re-route's TRAP side is closed on all five bits that can vary there
 238: (MODE trapfrozenuser -- uniquely, per CTL_RRTRAPINV; SFD1 trapfrozensfd1 AND trapfrozenuser, which clears both bits;
 239: IND trapfrozenind, C trapfrozenc, SER trapfrozenser; SFRZ is invariant BY CONSTRUCTION, since it is the guard) -- v17 closed three of those five and left MODE and SFD1, and pass 11 graded that
 240: L2 rather than debt on two precedents from this round's own records.  What remains
 241: disclosed: MULTI-AXIS joints of two or more PSR bits at one arm (clause (e) by the carrier's own bound), and vectors 0..3
 242: (m88kexchwtraps).
