C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\fablequeue7n_20261009\fable5_rule7n_35.md:6:7n-5 VERDICT: NO -- "closable by a finite row set" is not the discriminator and was already rejected on 2026-09-04 ("a C int is finite; finiteness does no bounding work"); each single slice is one-row closable and the FAMILY of slices never is, in BOTH of the round's buckets, so finiteness separates nothing.  The governing discriminator is what the BODY TESTS AS A CASE (joint-cells 09-04, D1 09-25), under which the tile-index escapes, the TLB-contents slice and the value slices are ONE species, clause (e).  The TLB-array-contents gap is coverage DEBT (one readback, filed at the top of this file's debt), not L2 and not a repair owing a pass; the committed controlling contract (probe `:26-62`, 2026-09-12) already says so ("OUTSIDE: ... tile indices, descriptor payloads"), and the row note, the probe's historical block and the pass-2 receipt contradict it -- three L4s.  EXHAUSTED/SAMPLED is ADOPTED as clause-(e) disclosure vocabulary with one definitional correction (EXHAUSTED = every cell of the body-tested partition rowed, never "every value in the domain").
C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\fablequeue7n_20261009\fable5_rule7n_35.md:64:* **The doctrinal half was decided on 2026-09-25**, after this question was filed: the flagship D1 ruling on `#549` v6 pinned *"'TESTS' MEANS MASKS OR COMPARES AS A CASE, NOT 'DEPENDS ON'"* -- a relational compare "tests NO bit: its generating set is its three regions, below / at / past the bound", a slice of a compared value crossed with a floor cell is clause (e), and *"grading by consequence would reopen #548"*.  7n-5 asks whether a data-flow test ("flows into the address operand") promotes an untested input to a floor axis; D1 answers no, two weeks after the question.
C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\fablequeue7n_20261009\fable5_rule7n_35.md:65:* **The instance half was decided on 2026-09-12 by the committed probe itself.**  `regress/sgi_re_colourdefault_probe.py:26-28`: *"CONTRACT -- #519 closure design, 2026-09-12.  This is the controlling coverage contract; older CONTRACT/CLOSED/COMPLETE claims below are historical and are superseded wherever they claim a larger domain or describe missing coverage."*  `:50-51`: *"OUTSIDE: exhaustive coordinates, tile indices, descriptor payloads, raw mode bits, foreground values ..."* -- descriptor payloads ARE the TLB array contents.  The controlling contract already files the gap as clause (e).
C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\fablequeue7n_20261009\fable5_rule7n_35.md:77:**The governing discriminator is the one the carrier already carries, read with its bounds.**  (i) Clause (d)'s operand-swap enumeration draws swaps from *fields the guarded BODY READS*, walked up only to the enclosing-function boundary: here `tileptr`, `ofs`, `buf`, `bufdepth`.  Those swaps were all killed at 59 rows (`ok || ofs` 58/59 by `ycrcb x4y1`; `ok || tileptr` by every decline row, since `tileptr` is nonzero everywhere).  (ii) The CELLS owed are the cross-product of the guard's dominating predicates with the body-TESTED partitions of the device-state lvalues the repair path reads (pass 11, 09-04), where "tests" means masks or compares as a case (D1, 09-25).  (iii) A value, bit or slice the body never tests as a case is clause (e), disclosed; consequence orders the debt queue and never promotes to floor (D1: `#549`'s latch x bit was graded (e) although its consequence was the round's own defect).
C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\fablequeue7n_20261009\fable5_rule7n_35.md:89:**So the measuring seat's FLOOR grade of the tile-index family was wrong AS A GRADE, and the codex class-closure review of 2026-09-11 was right** (*"BECAUSE THE BODY NEVER TESTS `tile_nr` FOR ZERO, `M30` ... IS NOT A FLOOR AXIS UNDER THE BODY-TESTED-PARTITION RULE -- IT IS CLAUSE-(e) DEBT"*).  The data-flow sentence the seat used (*"flows into the address operand at least as directly as `tlb_mode` does"*) is the 2026-09-09 LABEL clause with its first half dropped: a dispatch LABEL becomes a floor axis when its value flows into a body-read lvalue -- `tlb_mode` is a label the body tests as a case AND flows into `tileptr`; `tile_nr` flows and is not tested as a case.  Flow alone is the transitive-chasing reading the 08-24 bound forbids.
C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\fablequeue7n_20261009\fable5_rule7n_35.md:95:**EXHAUSTED / SAMPLED: ADOPTED as clause-(e) disclosure vocabulary, with one correction.**  It is exactly what clause (e) asks for -- *"write into the CONTRACT which cells are covered and which are deliberately not"* -- made explicit per axis.  Definitions: EXHAUSTED := every cell of the BODY-TESTED partition of that lvalue is rowed (floor discharged on that axis); SAMPLED := driven at two or more values, with the untested slices and their derived or measured sweeps named.  The probe's `:587` wording "every value in the reachable domain is driven" coincides with the partition definition for `tlb_mode`/`bufdepth`/`color_mode` (tiny domains) and must not be the definition: the next probe with a 2^32 operand could never write EXHAUSTED under it and would write it anyway for a 16-value field the body tests at one bound.  BOUND: a disclosure vocabulary can never DEMAND a row (the carrier's filter rule: *"a filter can reject or repair a row; it can never demand a new one"*), so it cannot grow.  STRUCTURAL LANDING SPOT, per the structure-first rule: the PRETABLE block's GUARD FIELD vs BODY FIELD check gains one column, "partition the BODY induces on this lvalue" (the codex 09-11 table is the exemplar), and EXHAUSTED/SAMPLED is read off that column rather than asserted.  A template line, not a checker.
C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\fablequeue7n_20261009\fable5_rule7n_35.md:101:3. **Released:** the repair pass the queue entry said the TLB-contents gap "owes"; any class-closure demand over `(x, y)`.
C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\fablequeue7n_20261009\fable5_rule7n_35.md:102:4. **Carrier, one sentence under the joint-cells clause, with the structural column above:** *"A derived input (a local computed from the function's inputs and feeding a body-read operand) is graded by the partition the body induces on IT, never by the flow that reaches it: `#519`'s `tile_nr`, tested only at `< 256`, is clause (e); the finite-row-set warrant is the 09-04 finiteness bound and buys nothing in either direction."*
