C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\asiceventaddr\pass1_20261009\fable5_pass1.md:13:PREMISE WRONG: section 8(d) says (a), (d) and (f) are "clause-(e) disclosures, not floor -- right?" and stops there.  Half right: none of the three is in the DEPENDS-ON closure, but (a) and (d) are MEASURED escapes of an UNSHIPPED detector, which is L1 (pre-ship construction), and one row at 256 kills both (RAN).  (f) stays clause (e) pending D2.  And the list omits the one candidate that IS in the closure: (g) is "a condition qualified" on the dominating predicate and is FLOOR.
C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\asiceventaddr\pass1_20261009\fable5_pass1.md:51:Warrant: DEPENDS-ON enumerates the predicates dominating the diff's edited lines within the enclosing construct (here the macro set), and the 2026-09-25 pin says a relational compare's generating set is its three regions.  The two compares are `(e) >= 0` and `(e) < 96`; regions: lower {-1 below, 0 at, >0 past}, upper {<96 below, 96 at, >96 past}.  {0, 95, 96, 128, -1} covers all six (95 serves both "past the lower bound" and "below the upper bound").  The (d)-closure mutants -- noguard, null, each single relaxation/tightening of either compare, `* 0` -> `* 1`, the argument replaced by a constant -- are all killed (RAN).  The body's own tests on `e`: ADDR tests nothing (a shift), BITMASK masks `& 31` as a VALUE, not as a case -- no joint cell, no disagreeing-state row (guard and body read the same single lvalue).  The device switch's bands are a CALLEE's tests: clause (e), as the brief says.  **So yes, that set + RT + ID is the floor -- with two additions the floor itself demands and the brief's list lacks:**
C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\asiceventaddr\pass1_20261009\fable5_pass1.md:60:(iii) **Under D2, yes, 97 is owed; 1 is not.**  Lower bound: `>= 0 -> >= 1` is killed by A0 and `>= 0 -> >= -1` by Xm1 (RAN), so the near rows on both sides already exist (-1, 0).  Upper bound: 95 and 96 are the near rows; 128 pins the "past" BRANCH, and only 97 pins the BOUND against (f).  (f) is a two-term composite, not a single relaxation, so it is outside the (d) closure -- clause (e) -- and it is D2's first instance.  My recommendation independent of D2: add X97 under L1 (one `-DCASE`, measured kill of (f)), and KEEP X128 as the device-anchored "first address that would clobber a mask register" row.  The ruling on D2 as a rule is the owner's; this round can carry its instance either way.
