C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\crimewidthkill\repair16_f2_20260926\fable5_f2_adjudication.md:5:**VERDICT: THE CHAIN CLOSES ON THIS PASS -- zero floor breaches survive adjudication on a valid, full-roster pass; repair 16's rows all stand; NO row is owed. Two of the main loop's GRADES are overturned without moving a row: the latch-gated clears (X3) and the bit-conditioned clears (X1) are both clause (e) -- the CONTROL arm distinguishes neither the latch nor bit 0 -- so the deleted clause-(e) sentence goes back and the "closes the residue-text channel AS A CLASS" heading comes out (it is true of the COUNT for the arm's TESTED bits, false of the value axis and of the print channel). ENDIANESS stays clause (e) and its rows stay as a licensed strengthening. Seven L4 record corrections land in the probe's text before the base leg is re-run on the final bytes; every strengthening named by any seat is FILED, none is in-round. Astra confirms; nothing commits before #549.**
C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\crimewidthkill\repair16_f2_20260926\fable5_f2_adjudication.md:20:**X2 (F2/D4, the ENDIANESS counts) -- UPHOLD the rows, REFINE the contract; minimax/deepseek OVERTURNED.** ENDIANESS is cleared unconditionally and never branched on: clause (e), exactly as my pass 2 and the 09-25 re-ruling graded it -- so it is NOT a member of the tested-bit class and the contract must not list it as one. But "not owed" does not mean "not allowed": the addition licence governs product code, the floor rules bound what a filter may DEMAND, and repair 14's ruling C is in-round precedent for rowing above the floor. The ENDIANESS catch is inseparable from the ten-write aggregate (you cannot count the latch-SET DOG cell over ACCEPTS without counting 0x0100), it has a measured delta (table 15a escape -> table 16's two exact reds), and its cost -- a full re-table -- was paid. Licensed strengthening, labelled as one.
C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\crimewidthkill\repair16_f2_20260926\fable5_f2_adjudication.md:22:**X3 (F4/D3, the latch-gated clears) -- OVERTURN the grade; the rows stay.** "The CONTROL arm reads no latch" IS the clause-(e) test: DEPENDS-ON enumerates a joint only where the guarded body's own code distinguishes the operand, and the arm distinguishes `writeflag`, DOG and HARD_RESET -- never `d->warned`. The latch is a floor axis of the GOTO (via the label the switch re-tests after the join), not of the arm's residue. glm's objection -- the reason "describes the fixed build, not the space of edits" -- proves too much: every clause-(e) disposition describes the fixed build; the bound exists so the enumeration is finite. `L_dogclr` and `D_dogbit0` are the same shape (one conjunct the arm does not test, on the same clear); the main loop disclosed one and rowed the other as if owed. Both are clause (e). `rearm ctl msg` and `rst 4w/8w msg` remain as licensed strengthenings (measured: 225/226 and 224/226; dependent kills re-run). The deleted sentence returns, corrected to say the cell is rowed anyway.
C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\crimewidthkill\repair16_f2_20260926\fable5_f2_adjudication.md:38:1. **My pass-2 L2 grade for `H_noresetclear` rests on SIBLING PARITY with a channel-validity ruling, not on a floor clause as written.** The 13/17 conditional made the DOG pair owed because the accepted 0x0200 cell's ONLY observable was the text count; the accepted 0x0800 cells already had a varying channel (the halt, K_ctl4w/8w_reset_post). I extended L2 to the HARD_RESET clear by analogy -- HARD_RESET is a partition the arm TESTS -- and the round accepted it. The repair is right and cheap and no seat disputes it; but the contract must cite that warrant (13/17 + parity over the arm's tested bits) rather than invent a class. And it draws the line for X3 exactly: a TESTED partition earns parity; an UNTESTED conjunct (the latch, bit 0) is clause (e). One step further and it is #392.
C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\crimewidthkill\repair16_f2_20260926\fable5_f2_adjudication.md:49:**Surviving floor breaches: NONE.** Each candidate this pass raised is graded above: X1 clause (e) by #549 D1; X3 clause (e) by the joint-cells bound; `M_ctldebug` a channel-transport disclosure, not a (d) mutant of the fix; `ctlrst sw halt`'s missing kill a records defect, now discharged by a measured kill. The stop condition -- zero breaches surviving adjudication on a valid pass, with the enumeration -- is met.
C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\crimewidthkill\repair16_f2_20260926\fable5_f2_adjudication.md:56:2. **Latch joints (X3).** "THE LATCH IS NOT AN AXIS OF THIS ARM: the CONTROL arm reads no latch (`d->warned` has one reader and one writer, both in the decline block), so a clear gated on it is clause (e) -- ROWED ANYWAY: `rearm ctl msg` (DOG, latch SET; L_dogclr 225/226) and `rst 4w/8w msg` (HARD_RESET, latch SET; L_rstclr 224/226)."
C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\crimewidthkill\repair16_f2_20260926\fable5_f2_adjudication.md:57:3. **ENDIANESS (X2).** "ENDIANESS (0x0100) is cleared unconditionally and never branched on: clause (e), NOT a member of the tested-bit class. Its clear skipped (E_noendianclear: 218/218 on repair 15, 224/226 here) is carried as a SIDE EFFECT of the ten-write aggregate counts, a strengthening and not a floor claim."
