C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\wdc473floor\r3pass_20261013\fable5\fable5_r3pass.md:5:VERDICT: BREACH (edit: dev_wdc.c:1228, the read arm's branch `if (d->atapi_cmd_in_progress)` -> `if (d->atapi_st != NULL)` -- a clause-(2) operand swap of a dominating predicate to a field its guarded body reads, never built in any of the 254 runs, and passing all 159 rows BY READING of every data-port read site; input: any dispatched packet command (TEST UNIT READY), then an ATA command that loads the ring (ATAPI IDENTIFY DEVICE 0xA1, or READ SECTORS to the other drive on the channel), then ONE 16-bit DATA read -- HEAD leaves INTRQ unasserted, the mutant asserts it after that read and after every later one; row owed: the PIO row re-run with a transfer object hanging off the device, `d.atapi_st = scsi_transfer_alloc()` before the 1024-byte preload, the idiom `row_stale_phase_write` already uses for the SAME swap on the write side -- the mutant reads a255 = 255 where HEAD reads 0.)  Second, on grade not on measurement: the survivor `n_F_VD1_width1_consumes2` is DISPUTED as clause (e) -- the body test that distinguishes the width-1 cell is the handler's own `len >= 2 ? 2 : 1` (dev_wdc.c:1255); the one width-1 row's channel (occupancy, constant fill) cannot vary under it, so the cell is rowed and unobserved; one count read after a 1-byte DATA read closes it.  The chain does NOT close on this pass.
C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\wdc473floor\r3pass_20261013\fable5\fable5_r3pass.md:92:**(e) DISPUTED -- n_F_VD1_width1_consumes2 (`consumed = len == 4 ? 4 : 2`).**  The question as the brief puts it: name the body test that tests that cell as a case.  It is the SAME line that settles C6 the other way: `int consumed = len == 4 ? 4 : (len >= 2 ? 2 : 1);` (:1255).  `len >= 2` distinguishes width 1 as its own case exactly as it fails to distinguish width 8.  `len` is a function INPUT the guarded body reads directly, not a derived local; the 2026-10-09 ruling grades a DERIVED local (`consumed`) by the tests on IT, and does not demote the tests the body performs on the input that computes it.  Under the JOINT rule ("the PARTITION the body's own tests induce") the body-induced partition on `len` is {<2, >=2 and !=4, 4}; under the committed generating-set clause ("every idata bit the guarded body TESTS is written both clear and set" -- for a relational compare, its regions) the region below `len >= 2`'s bound must be driven at a floor cell WITH A CHANNEL; and the CHANNEL line says the one width-1 row (`write route: 1-byte store is refused`, 32768 width-1 reads at :7160-7161) is vacuous for this mutant -- it reads occupancy and a constant 0xc3 fill, which VD1 cannot move, as the contract itself records.  So the cell is driven and unobserved: a floor cell with no live row, not a disclosure.  Guest-visible consequence (REASONED): a driver reading an N-byte DATA-IN with byte-wide loads (legal on every CPU here) sees `atapi_len` fall by 2 per byte -- after N/2 reads the command COMPLETES with N/2 bytes still queued (ireason 0x03, count 0, an interrupt), and each further byte read re-runs the completion and re-asserts the interrupt.  First distinguishing input: arm any DATA-IN (INQUIRY, 36 bytes), ONE 8-bit DATA read, then read CYL_LO: HEAD 35 (0x23), VD1 34 (0x22).  Row owed (one line, L2 if the grade is upheld, L1 otherwise): in `write_route_case(..., 1, ...)` read CYL_LO/CYL_HI after the first 1-byte read and want 32767 -- or a two-call leg: arm 4 bytes, one 1-byte read, want count 3 and phase DATAIN (VD1: 2, and on a 2-byte arm COMPLETED).  I grade it FLOOR; the adjudicator may read 7n-5 the other way -- but then the record must say the cell is body-distinguished and SAMPLED-unobserved, not "a value the body never tests".
