C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\mapledmaaddr\fable_pass1_20260912.md:9:**VERDICT: ACCEPT upheld, 9/9 by argument as well as by count. The FAULT member is UNAVAILABLE on SH4 and its idiom is a silent load-skip — that goes into the CHANGELOG *and* corrects the carrier's member-5 clause. Floor = (a)(b)(c) + the accept cell with a POISONED destination + silence over the whole read interval + `other read` (the dominating-predicate complement); everything keyed on a `dmaaddr` value — zero, `== 0x04`, all-ones, the read-to-clear double read — is clause (e), taken as L1 because cheap, never graded floor. The DMA leg is NOT floor: it kills only a new lvalue outside the BOUND; defer it to `mapledmaadvance` with a no-row sentence, or if shipped here, L1 with the refusal-message `E` as its only admissible oracle. The agy witness is ADMISSIBLE as the rung-3 test-first witness (4/12 → 12/12, same script, both controls), but its `read quiet` row is CHANNEL-invalid and must not be carried into the detector unchanged.** Evidence basis: 7/7 scriptable seats, Opus, and agy (fired for measurement, not reading). I read the tree; built nothing.
C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\mapledmaaddr\fable_pass1_20260912.md:13:**Q2 — row list, under my xscaleinten Q1 rule** (*"the floor is clause (b) verbatim reinstatement plus the dominating predicates' accept cell; every re-introduction keyed on a body-read operand the body does not test (`rd == k`, `field & bit`, `field == v`) is clause (e), disclosed BY CLASS; any row added for one is L1 — licensed because cheap, never graded floor because cheap"*). The body `odata = d->dmaaddr;` tests nothing; dominating predicates `relative_addr == 0x04`, `writeflag != MEM_WRITE`.
C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\mapledmaaddr\fable_pass1_20260912.md:17:- **Double read, no write between (glm, Opus): clause (e), L1.** Read-to-clear ADDS a store to a state lvalue; it is neither a predicate weakening nor an operand swap. One extra load — take it, and the contract states "reads have no side effect".
C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\mapledmaaddr\fable_pass1_20260912.md:19:- **codex's `d->dmaaddr == 0x04`: clause (e), the `idata == k` shape — NOT floor.** This is `rd == 0` with the constant inherited from `relative_addr == 0x04` by coincidence, exactly the reading I overturned this morning: *"floor membership [would] depend on which constant the sibling dispatch happened to carry."* `d->dmaaddr` is a state lvalue, which `rd` was not — but the body tests no partition of it, so its partition is one class and `== 0x04` is `field == v` by the rule's own text. Codex's "reuses existing constants, not arbitrary sweeps" is the coincidence argument restated. A value-4 row costs one write; take it as L1 if wanted; disclose `== k` by class.
