C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\lcaisalane\opus_c4_20260914\OPUS_ANSWER.md:1:# VERDICT: GAP -- read arm, after its forward: `if (len != 1) cpu->memory_rw(cpu, cpu->mem, LCA_ISA_BASE + relative_addr, &byte, 1, MEM_READ, CACHE_NONE);` (R2w). It scores **111/111** (`logs/probe_R2w.raw`) and changes what the guest sees: an **LDL** of IIR 0x3fa with TXRDY armed delivers lane-2 IIR & 3 = **0x1 instead of 0x2** (`logs/disc2_R2w.out`). That is the contract-named RD2 edit, gated on exactly the one width its single row uses. Four more edits of the same forward-count class also score 111/111 and are guest-visible, all MEASURED: **WT6/WTsplit** (the split-TAIL write cells), **RD2L0** (lane-0 reads) and **L3gate** (lane-3 direct, whose header warrant is false again). The next repair owes the whole-class closure tabled in Q1.
C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\lcaisalane\opus_c4_20260914\OPUS_ANSWER.md:200:**Cheapest whole-class closure: one diff, new sessions only, so no earlier kill moves.**
C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\lcaisalane\opus_c4_20260914\OPUS_ANSWER.md:255:* The header's data-class disclosure names *mis-decode* keyed on data.  **It should also name the fallthrough keyed on data**, or the class-closure repair should close it for free with nonzero stub stores (above).
C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\mapledmaaddr\fable_close_20260912.md:45:**Disclosing it is the RIGHT grade, and it is forced, not chosen.** A session has no terminal event in *emulated* time (unlike process exit), so free-running F ticks only moves the boundary to F — the axis is unbounded and cannot be closed into a floor. The carrier lists "effects keyed on the environment (time, ...)" as clause (e) precisely for this. Grading it floor would be the unbounded-row-growth (#392) shape.
C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\mapledmaaddr\fable_close_20260912.md:54:- **(b) atexit / time-axis** — split, and the split is the point: the HOST-process-exit `atexit` announce (`M_ATEXIT`, 36/37) is a FLOOR breach (a diagnostic shape, now in-window because the transcript reads through EOF), caught, **L1**; the EMULATED-time-beyond-span periodic report (`M_TICKPERIODIC4`, 37/37) is **clause (e), DISCLOSED window** — correctly NOT floor, and it MUST survive (a kill would mean the window is narrower than stated and the record wrong).
C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\mapledmaaddr\fable_close_20260912.md:57:- **(e) proportion — NOT fully proportionate, and partly my fault.** Seven tables for a two-line ACCEPT fix, almost all on the silence oracle. The honest split: tables 3→4→5 were a cell-by-cell grind on ONE class (a whitelist oracle has a shape to hide in — literal → grammar → count → exemption), and the class-closure amendment ("two consecutive passes finding one class → close the whole space in ONE diff") should have short-circuited that directly into table 6's whole-transcript-through-EOF model. Table 5 was worse than idle: it *regressed* the class onto a new time axis. Tables 6→7 were legitimate — the emulated-time axis is a genuinely new, unbounded axis that required Opus's tick-ladder to discover and bound, and the floor-channel hardenings (full-line disasm, exit0, EOF) could NOT be filed because they are floor breaches. **Net ≈ two avoidable tables (4,5).** It could not have "disclosed earlier and filed the rest" for the in-band channel — that channel is floor. The durable lesson is structural and already a CHECKPOINT candidate: **build a silence oracle as an exact whole-transcript compare from the start, never iterate up from a whitelist.**
C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\mapledmaaddr\fable_close_20260912.md:61:**My pass-2 §Q3 closure PRESCRIPTION was wrong, and the round adopted it as table 5.** I wrote: *"Closure, in one diff: (i) `session()` snapshots the buffer BEFORE it writes `quit` and `noise()` reads the snapshot — then no exemption is needed."* That snapshot is exactly what created the atexit/time blind spot Opus measured in the closing pass (`M_ATEXIT` 37/37). I correctly diagnosed the disease — *a count with an exemption is a whitelist* — and then prescribed a cure that **generalised the one-line exemption (`GXemul> quit`) into an unbounded time window after the snapshot.** The correct closure was table 6's, which Opus stated against me directly: *"the fix is to MODEL that echo, not to stop short of it"* — read the FULL transcript through EOF and model the `quit` echo. This is the sharpest thing in the round: the seat holding the class-closure gavel handed the round a repair that reproduced the class on a new axis. It is the #499 shape (a breach reproduced inside its own repair) arriving from the adjudicator's chair, and it cost table 5's entire pass.
C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\mapledmaaddr\fable_close_20260912.md:63:Everything else of mine held and was adopted correctly: D1 (alignment is a clause-(e) value cell of the body-read field, not "outside the BOUND" — the header now says so, and the old L4 sentence is gone), D2 (`case 0x00` is FLOOR via the eight-cell single-bit selector generating set — all eight now rowed), F3/F5 (the two (e) sub-reasons stated separately), and the HOLD-for-class-closure itself. I checked the header for any residual overclaim: the unqualified "ANY ... printed late" that Opus graded L4 is corrected to the stated window; "however long it waits" now correctly refers to HOST-exit handlers, which red via `unclean()` even when their output is never read, and is distinguished from the emulated-time disclosure.
C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\fbd5\p1_20260919\FABLE_P1_ANSWER.md:19:What it discharges: `m_swallow` and the store-into-status class become MEASURED KILLS (seed `irq_status = 0x10`, `irq_enable = 0x30`; a constant-0 read arm and a `&=`-style store both red) -- coverage, not disclosure. What it only NARROWS: `m_fiqraw`. Seeding `fiq_status` pins the read EXPRESSION against a field no product code writes; the disclosure "no guest can reach a nonzero FIQ status" stays in clause (e) verbatim. The contract must name the split exactly as C2 says: guest rows = reachability, survival, latch count, TEXT; differential rows = preservation, expression.
