C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\lcaisalane\f2_8bd97e4_20260918\panel_20260918_190129\fable5_f2.md:33:The panel is right that E-DEBT-PLUS-L4 does not survive, and I verified the mechanism rather than counting the 8–0: `vc = && (len<=8 || (P&3)==3)` scores **frozen 3/3** because lane 3 keeps `(P&3)==3` true (forwards `s[3]=0x44`), and **l0w16 2/3** because lane 0 makes it false at `len=16>8`, dropping the store into the read arm (SCR keeps its preset). That is a *per-lane null of the repair, invisible at the lane the row occupies* — the `sgimtedepth4dead` `&& dst_tlb==MTE_TLB_A` shape exactly, and `#499`'s "repaired at the address the mutant used." Lane is the guard operand's body-distinguished partition (`byte = data[ofs]`, `ofs = P&3`), so by the 09-09 amendment `{write guard} × {lane 0-3}` is floor. **L2, class closure owed.**
C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\lcaisalane\f2_8bd97e4_20260918\panel_20260918_190129\fable5_f2.md:39:- **{mc2, kbc1024} as the closure (agy, deepseek, minimax, and your filed pair)** is a covering, not a closure — and grok and glm proved it with a checkable mutant: `&& (len<=8 || (P&3)!=1)`, the *same clause-(d) form as vc*, passes both sessions, because `mc2` drives lanes 2/3 and `kbc1024` drives lane 0 — **neither drives lane 1 at a wide width.** Only `low16` (8259 IMR, port 0x21, lane 1) reds it. Shipping that pair as "class closure" replays `#499` at lane 1 on the next pass. This is the sharpest thing on the table and only grok/glm/codex reached it.
