C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\m88kexcdeliver\pass1\opus_p1.md:280:I confirmed by execution that `VERBOSITY_ERROR` lines print at default verbosity (the probe passes no verbosity flag; `-V` is the debugger switch). So under D1-as-written, **every delivered exception prints an ERROR line**, and on a booted guest a userland divide-by-zero would emit one per SIGFPE. I also measured the *flood*: 25 and 28 repeats respectively before `running = false` takes effect, because the dyntrans loop runs `N_SAFE_DYNTRANS_LIMIT` instructions between checks. **Two arguments for INFO:** parity with the four already-implemented classes, and the fact that a routine guest-handled trap is not an emulator error. **I found no hygiene-gate row keying on these lines** (`grep 'exception' regress/gate_hygiene.sh` returns one unrelated comment at `:92`), so nothing reds either way — which makes `M_LEVEL` genuinely **DISCLOSED under clause (e)**, and the brief is right about that one.
