C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\pcc2c040kill\assertrow_review_20261009\fable5_ruling_v2_20261009.md:31:Why it is floor, not debt. The table's claim is "with C040 set, the line is not asserted." That claim has exactly two input cases -- something pending, nothing pending -- and the table pins only the first. The second is the device's reset state (IPL 0, MASK 0, no INT bits): a single byte store of 0x06 to GENCTL in a fresh machine reaches it, which makes it MORE reachable than the rowed case, not less. X is a one-token change to the repair's own assignment that is wrong in half of that assignment's reachable domain. That is a mutation of the repair, not of some remote input, and its guest-visible consequence (a spurious interrupt while C040 is set) is the exact behaviour the fix exists to prevent, reached from the idle side instead of the pending side. [Clause (d): guard kept, repair perverted. The joint cell {C040 set} x {assert entering = 0}: `assert` is the repair's write target and the function's own `if (assert)` three lines below splits it {0, nonzero}, so the 2x2 is the diff-closed floor; (clear,1), (set,1) and clear-after-set are rowed, (set,0) is the open symmetric cell -- the #499 shape. The "derived local, data-flow chasing" reading that would make it clause (e) fails because `assert` is not an upstream input chased through the function; it is the variable the repair writes, consumed by the next statement.]
C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\pcc2c040kill\assertrow_review_20261009\fable5_ruling_v2_20261009.md:39:Why it is debt, not floor. This arm's code reads and tests exactly one bit of `warned`; the other bits belong to other arms, and the once-ness of those arms is pinned by their own rows (pcc2_width_probe.py), not by the C040 table. The C040 table's obligation on `warned` is the C040 bit in both states, and both are held (`c040 once`, `c040 predirty`). Outbound damage to bits this arm never reads is outside what this detector promises. [The DEPENDS-ON bound stops at the enclosing function and at fields the guarded body reads; bits the body never tests are marginals, clause (e). The shared-bitfield question -- "who else writes this field, can they set my bit" -- is the inbound direction and is rowed; the outbound direction is this, and a write-time check can reject or repair a row but never demand one.] It is still a real one-token hazard with a real consequence, so: file it MED, disclose it in the probe's contract (the contract does not currently mention it), and the pin is the re-fire row.
