C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\pcc2widthkills\pass10_seats_20260904\fable\FINDINGS.md:17:**RULE RULING:** The **dissent's core reasoning FAILS** — its plausibility test is the wrong discriminator, and its claim "read as single-operand, the closure is complete" is **measurably false** (`&& idata != 2` is a single-operand form on a body-read lvalue that clean-sweeps 194/194 and is disclosed, not killed). The **main loop's DISPOSITION (ship the row) is RIGHT**, but its **proposed bound is self-refuting**: "PAIRS … where a cell is a reachable guest state" would force rowing `idata==2`, `TxICR 0x37` and `TxCTL 0xff` (all reachable guest states) that the same record *discloses*. Neither side's stated rule is adoptable. The principled, finite, derivable discriminator that includes `pendboth` and excludes `idata!=2` is: **a joint/multi-lvalue cell is in clause (d) exactly when the guarded body's OWN CODE tests that combination (each lvalue at a partition it distinguishes, read together in one operation); cells the body never distinguishes are disclosed under clause (e).** Keep the row; adopt that rule; add ONE contract sentence stating the discriminator. A closing pass cannot assert "zero floor breaches surviving adjudication" while the floor's own scope is this pass's open question.
C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\pcc2widthkills\pass10_seats_20260904\fable\FINDINGS.md:29:1. *"`&& !(p1 && p2)` is not an edit anyone writes."* Wrong discriminator. The project's own class-closure amendment ("THE AMENDMENT THAT ACTUALLY ENDS CHAINS") is exactly this shape: *"a cell of one state space left empty … leaving the symmetric cell open … enumerate the full space from the function's own inputs, close every cell in ONE diff."* Three pending cells (neither / T1-only / T2-only) were pinned; the symmetric `(+,+)` was left open. `#499`'s cells were adjudicated by reachability-of-a-symmetric-cell, **not** by plausibility-of-expression. Point 1 is refuted by the carrier the main loop cites.
C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\pcc2widthkills\pass10_seats_20260904\fable\FINDINGS.md:46:> *Clause (d)'s DEPENDS-ON closure includes a JOINT cell over two or more of {the guard's operands, the lvalues the guarded body reads} exactly when the guarded body's OWN CODE distinguishes that cell — it tests each lvalue at the partition the cell fixes (e.g. `pending > 0`) and reads them together in one statement or semantic operation. The enumerated cells are the CROSS-PRODUCT of those per-lvalue body-tested partitions — never arbitrary boolean functions of the read-set — and a mutant exempting any single cell whose reachability is MEASURED is a floor breach. Close the whole cross-product in ONE diff and state in the contract which cells are rowed and which disclosed. A value or bit-combination the body never tests as a case (`idata == k`; a byte no conditional distinguishes) is disclosed under clause (e); a cell no access reaches is disclosed by name.*

